Reading command output that is an incomplete UTF-8 byte (a lone 0xC3 lead byte)
inserts zero runes, exercising readio's empty-loginsert and trailing partial-rune
(b!=0 -> nulls) handling and the "null characters elided" warning.

-- stdin --
,<printf '\303'
,p
-- input --
hello
-- stderr --
 -. input
?warning: null characters elided
!
?changed files
